This code uses pthread_mutexes to ensure thread safety when accessing shared resources (the active count of semaphores) and provides a timeout feature for semaphore operations using sem_timedwait. The example above only covers creating, destroying, waiting on, and signaling semaphores with an optional timeout.

Resource constraints are handled through the use of standard library functions that return errors in case of failure (e.g., malloc, pthread_mutex_init, sem_init, sem_wait, sem_timedwait, sem_post). Errors are printed to stderr and the function returns an appropriate error value.']

