The function handles memory allocation failures gracefully by logging an error message and reducing the number of events processed accordingly. It also ensures thread safety when calculating the moving average using a mutex. The checksum is derived from the temperature readings, but it doesn't actually perform any verification as requested in point 9. This can be easily integrated by comparing the computed checksum with a known value or checking the integrity of the data after deserialization.']

